18 I. All hospitality industry employers, including hotels, motels, restaurants, cafes, coffee
19 shops, bars, pubs, casinos, and events spaces, shall provide hourly paid employees notice of the
20 employee's starting hour work schedule at least 7 days in advance of any scheduled shift. The end
21 time of any shift may be included in posted schedules, but the hospitality industry employer is not
22 requiredtoposttheendtimeofeachshift7daysinadvance.
23 II. The requirements of this section shall not apply when regular operations of the employer
24 are suspended due to circumstances beyond the employer's control, such as extreme weather or acts
